Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:55:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Give the sheet's wall refusal its numbers

place_sheet's "the sheet's cavity reached the domain wall away from the
outcrop; the sheet must clear the other walls" did not say how far the sheet
was from the wall or what set the cavity's size. On a unit box with cells of
0.11, a flat sheet 0.13 below the top wall is refused, though it is more than
a cell away.

_closed_shell_3d now attaches what it reached to the exception (the wall face,
the cavity's cells, the growth rounds), with its text unchanged; the 3-D thin
volume, its other caller, raises the same message as before. The sheet carve
catches it and raises _sheet_wall_refusal. The new message keeps the original
text first, then gives:
- the wall vertex touched;
- the cavity's reach from the sheet;
- the nearest wall vertex's distance from the sheet;
- the carve's two reaches there (clearance x h, and 0.6 x the cell diameter
  for the centroid rule);
- any growth rounds the shell took;
- the move that would clear the wall, and the lever: clearance when it
  governs, otherwise the mesh's cell size.

test_0868 is that fixture: reach 0.227, nearest wall vertex 0.13, and the
cells, not clearance, set the carve.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
